Implementation: in dav.js, `davCfg()` returns defaults when nothing stored:

```js
const DAV_DEFAULTS = {
  url: "https://dav.jianguoyun.com/dav/",
  user: "13622913166@163.com",
  pass: "a4hepfmfcktpte4h",
};
function davCfg() {
  const stored = ...localStorage...;
  return { ...DAV_DEFAULTS, ...(stored || {}) };
}
```

So the app works out of the box; user can still override via settings.

Similarly The Odds API key default: the key is 401ac0d0bfe89e015aa8ca7c19dd56c6 — embedding it in the APK risks extraction/quota abuse, but it's a personal app and the user asked for defaults. They said "把启动配置默认填写进去" — 填写启动配置. Include the Odds API key too as default? The risk: APK decompilation reveals key; quota 500/month could be drained. But it's their personal app, low distribution. I'll include it as default too (config object), since user wants pre-filled. Actually let me be careful: I'll default the WebDAV creds (as asked) and also default the Odds API key (they'd want it; mention the risk).

Where to put defaults: dav.js DAV_DEFAULTS includes user/pass/url. For odds key: collector.js reads localStorage "nbaq:oddsapi-key" — add default fallback `DEFAULT_ODDS_KEY` in collector.js, and settings UI shows default as placeholder value.

Also: since defaults are baked in, davEnabled() should return true even without stored config (as long as defaults present) — in APK. In browser (PWA) still disabled due to CORS. So davEnabled = isApk() && cfg.user && cfg.pass.

